From: BRL-CAD developers <devs@brlcad.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Build both shared and static Clipper2 in bext

Pass -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON and -DCLIPPER2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS=ON to the
Clipper2 ExternalProject so bext installs both libClipper2.so and
libClipper2.a under the bundle prefix.

This makes the Clipper2Targets.cmake export set expose two CMake targets:

  Clipper2::Clipper2        (shared, PUBLIC dep for shared manifold)
  Clipper2::Clipper2-static (static, PRIVATE dep for static manifold)

Requires the companion clipper2_static_lib.patch to be applied to the
Clipper2 upstream first.

The bext manifold build (with bext_manifold_static.patch applied) then
passes Clipper2_ROOT to manifold so that manifold's find_package(Clipper2)
picks up the bundle-prefix install, giving manifold_static access to
Clipper2::Clipper2-static as a PRIVATE link dependency.

Applies to: BRL-CAD/bext, main branch (clipper2/CMakeLists.txt)
--- a/clipper2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/clipper2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@ if (ENABLE_CLIPPER2)
     CMAKE_ARGS
     ${BUILD_TYPE_SPECIFIER}
+    -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON
+    -DCLIPPER2_BUILD_STATIC_LIBS=ON
     -DCLIPPER2_UTILS=OFF
     -DCLIPPER2_TESTS=OFF
     -DCLIPPER2_EXAMPLES=OFF
